  partName: Left Front Bolt
  description: The Left Front Bolt is a tiny, complex-shaped fastener situated at
    the top-left-rear of the engine, fabricated from Material.001, playing a vital
    role in securing the engine's front section. Its high-strength material and precise
    threading enable it to withstand significant forces and stresses. Notably, the
    Left Front Bolt's location allows for easy access and maintenance, reducing downtime
    and repair costs.
